# Chaos: a dying creature fades out (O221; client/BASE.md "0139"; src/client/chaosdeathfade.h (new, pure), creature.h/.cpp,
# map.h/.cpp, mapview.cpp, luafunctions_client.cpp, mods/client_settings/classes/dataset.lua, options/graphics.otui; after 0001-0138).
# The stock client removes a creature from its tile in one frame when the server says it is gone. Now, when a creature is
# removed with 0 health, the map keeps a ghost of it: a copy of its last drawn frame, drawn at its tile with alpha going
# from 1 to 0 over 350 ms (smoothstep). The corpse is an ordinary item and appears at once as before; no server state, no
# delay of any gameplay, nothing waits for the fade.
#  * Map::removeThing: before the tile lets go of a creature, Creature::takeDeathGhost copies the outfit (without outline,
#    hit parts or shader), direction, walk phase, offsets, scale and position into a DeathGhost, when chaos::deathfade::
#    wantsGhost allows it: option on, not the local player, can be seen, 0 health, on a map tile. A creature that walks out of
#    view or steps has health, so it gets none. The ghost goes into Map::m_deathGhosts (chaosdeathfade.h GhostQueue).
#  * Bounds: at most 32 ghosts (the oldest is dropped), one per creature id, each dies after 350 ms (MapView::drawFloor
#    expires them), all cleared when the central floor changes, in Map::cleanDynamicThings (map clean, logout) and so with
#    the map. A ghost holds copies only, no Creature and no tile, so nothing can dangle.
#  * MapView::drawFloor: before the missiles of a floor, the ghosts of that floor are drawn with Creature::drawDeathGhost:
#    the same placement as Creature::draw (offsets, scale around the feet), the outfit queued with Outfit::draw and then
#    DrawQueue::setOpacity (the call the floor fading uses) over just those items. No light, no shadow, no name or bar.
#  * Creature.setDeathFade(bool) / isDeathFade() (static, one switch; default off in the engine, the overlay module
#    game_visualfx turns it on from the option).
#  * dataset.lua: option `deathFade` (default on); its apply tells game_visualfx (`onOption('deathFade', value)`).
#  * options/graphics.otui: a checkbox "Fade out dying creatures" under "Fade on floor change" (the panel grows 238 -> 257).
# Cost with no ghost: one empty() test per drawn floor and one flag test per removed creature. With ghosts: one outfit draw
# per ghost (up to 32, normally 1-5) for 350 ms.
# Known: layered outfits (a monster with colour templates) fade through the texture atlas, which uses the queue colour; when
# the atlas is full that one item is drawn without the fade. The ghost is drawn over the whole floor, not in the tile's
# painter order, so for 350 ms it may overlap a creature on a tile in front of it.
# Checked: applies after 0001-0138 on the base tree; the touched .cpp files pass g++ -fsyntax-only; the header passes its test.
# Not built, linked or run in a client; goes live with the next client build.
